  "term": "physiological arousal",
  "definition": "Physiological arousal is the body’s moment-to-moment level of activation, which can rise or fall during activities such as classroom learning. In this source, it is treated as a changing bodily state indexed through electrodermal measures like skin conductance and skin conductance response frequency.",
